From 69c9e5c98223c33a8956399ca774ce0d59a82731 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 354/488] soh: name the 18 address-named symbols defined in
 z_obj_bean.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 18 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Obj_Bean/z_obj_bean.c; updating their references touches 3 files in total.

  * D_80B90E30 -> sWateredBean
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the one bean plant that has been watered this
    frame; a bean claims the slot so only one plays the growth cutscene, and
    clears it when it despawns.

  * func_80B8EBC8 -> ObjBean_ResetGrowth
    deduced, confidence HIGH: zeroes the three growth angles and the sway
    offset, returning the plant to its ungrown state.

  * func_80B8EDF4 -> ObjBean_HidePlant
    deduced, confidence HIGH: zeroes the growth angles and scales the plant
    away entirely.

  * func_80B8EE24 -> ObjBean_GrowPlant
    deduced, confidence HIGH: advances the two growth angles toward their
    limits and drives the plant's scale from their sines, easing the sway
    offset back to centre.

  * func_80B8FE00 -> ObjBean_SetupSproutDelay
    deduced, confidence HIGH: shows the leaves and arms the 60-frame pause
    before the plant sprouts.

  * func_80B8FE3C -> ObjBean_SproutDelay
    deduced, confidence HIGH: waits out that pause.

  * func_80B8FE6C -> ObjBean_SetupSprout
    deduced, confidence HIGH: shows the leaves and soil together and starts
    the plant at a tiny scale.

  * func_80B8FEAC -> ObjBean_Sprout
    deduced, confidence HIGH: grows the plant to its full height and width,
    then moves on to the overshoot.

  * func_80B8FF50 -> ObjBean_SetupOvershoot
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the overshoot action at its starting
    angle.

  * func_80B8FF8C -> ObjBean_Overshoot
    deduced, confidence HIGH: stretches the plant past its final size on a
    sine and hands off to the settle once it passes the threshold.

  * func_80B90010 -> ObjBean_SetupSettle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs the settling action with its starting
    angle and decaying amplitude.

  * func_80B90050 -> ObjBean_Settle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: wobbles the plant's scale with a decaying
    oscillation and, once the amplitude runs out, hands it to the
    wait-for-water state.

  * func_80B908EC -> ObjBean_SetupWaitToFly
    deduced, confidence HIGH: hides the plant and installs the action that
    waits for the player to step off.

  * func_80B90918 -> ObjBean_WaitToFly
    deduced, confidence HIGH: once the player is off the leaf it rebuilds
    the path, moves the plant back to its start and hands off to the regrow
    delay.

  * func_80B90970 -> ObjBean_SetupRegrowDelay
    deduced, confidence HIGH: hides the plant, resets its scale and arms the
    100-frame pause before it grows back.

  * func_80B909B0 -> ObjBean_RegrowDelay
    deduced, confidence HIGH: holds that pause, restarting it whenever a
    horse tramples the patch.

  * func_80B909F8 -> ObjBean_SetupRegrow
    deduced, confidence HIGH: shows the plant again and arms the 30-frame
    regrow.

  * func_80B90A34 -> ObjBean_Regrow
    deduced, confidence HIGH: grows the plant back, re-enabling its
    collision, and returns it to waiting for the player once nothing is
    trampling it.

